<title>UK: London tea auction sees firm rates for landeds, of.</title>
<headline>London tea auction sees firm rates for landeds, of.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The London tea auction saw fair general demand for the 9,260 packages on offer, the official report said.</p>
<p>Last (1996) season Assams on offer sold well at firm rates, Bright East Africans were fully firm to dearer but mediums lost three to five pence, the report said.</p>
<p>Offshore teas met with good demand but prices moved lower.</p>
<p>The next auction will be on Monday, January 27.</p>
<p>-London Newsroom, +44 171 542 8071</p>
